The big thing about using a potion of slime as a weapon is there's a
certain risk to carrying them. First, to be an effective weapon of
death, you have to carry at least one in your main inventory, making
them rather dangerous when you're struck with certain wands. They're
twice as heavy as daggers, so you have to balance weight
considerations. You have to also  to consider which potions you should
turn to slime, which you alchemize, which you dilute for holy water.

On top of that, I don't think monster sliming ought to be
instantaneous. I see some monster code rewrites.

The Jar crashes over the pit fiend's head! The pit fiend doesn't look
very well -more-
The pit fiend jumps into a fire trap! -more-
The pit fiend looks much better.

And if you succeed, then you have slimes running around the level.
Maybe not as dangerous as an arch-lich, but definitely a danger if
you're not careful

Are named demons currently immune from sliming? Is Rodney? The Riders?



